<'per'='http://www.peregrine-cms.com/jcr/cms/1.0'>
<'nt'='http://www.jcp.org/jcr/nt/1.0'>

// The nodes INSIDE an object - collections and their rows. COPY at every
// level, against the folder types' inherited VERSION: these are parts of
// the record, not documents of their own. Under OPV=VERSION a checkin froze
// them as jcr:childVersionHistory references, so the published view of an
// object with a collection served the reference instead of the rows and the
// collection was empty on the public host. COPY snapshots the whole record
// into each version. The type is the DEFAULT below, so nodes the editor
// creates inside an object get copy semantics without asking for them.
[per:ObjectPart] > nt:unstructured
  orderable
  + * (nt:base) = per:ObjectPart copy

[per:Object] > nt:hierarchyNode, sling:OrderedFolder, per:Replication
  orderable
  + * (nt:base) = per:ObjectPart copy

